  "body": "Seen in a fresh sandbox HOME (only ~/.claude/settings.json) while writing the magpie-setup skill, on d2e0ea393 plus the skill's branch:\n\n```\n$ magpie library instructions set instr.txt\n✓ every agent already has it\n$ magpie library\nInstructions\n  1 lines → no agent\n```\n\nNo agent had been given the instructions, so nothing was written, and the line says the opposite. printLibraryResult in internal/cli/library_cli.go prints that whenever `res.Changed` is empty.\n\nThe same message after `magpie library mcp add <name> <url>` with no agents= is fixed in the commit that names this issue. Instructions have sets and per-agent state (InstructionsView), so the check there needs the agents the active set goes to. Expected: say the text is saved and given to no agent yet, and name `magpie library instructions agents <a,b…>`.",
