   "updated_at": "2026-10-25T17:37:00Z",
   "body": "The instructions half of the message fba554c7 fixed for `mcp add`: the saved text has no agent to go to, but `printLibraryResult` read the empty `res.Changed` as \"every agent already has it\".\n\nFixed on [fix/library-instructions-no-agent](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/library-instructions-no-agent) (`8977ba98`, based on today's `main`), following fba554c7's wording: after `instructions set` with no agent on the set, the command now says the text is in the library, given to no agent yet, and names `magpie library instructions agents <a,b…>`. Whether an agent is on it is read from `InstructionsView`, so an unchanged save with an agent on keeps the old line. An empty `set` (clearing the text) keeps the old line too.\n\n- Red → green: `TestLibraryInstructionsSetNoAgents` runs your sandbox sequence (fresh HOME with only `~/.claude/settings.json`, `set instr.txt`, then `agents claude`, then `set` again).\n- `internal/cli` + `internal/library` (`-tags nogui`): 789 passed.\n",
